// Written to answer one question honestly: does a real embedding model beat the
// local-hash-v2 sketch on this system? The scaffold this replaced could not answer it —
// EvalFixtures.isScaffold() exists because a corpus with uniform vocabulary makes every
// retrieval change look like an improvement.
//
// The structure that matters is the synonym-only pairs. Each has a target sharing no
// content word with its query, and a LEXICAL DECOY that does share the query's words, is
// semantically wrong, and is deliberately fresher and more accessed. BM25 and recency both
// point at the decoy. Only a semantic model can reach the target, so the two orderings
// separate cleanly instead of by luck.
//
// Not personal data. Whether a model finds paraphrases is a question about language.
